# Files whose *bytes* are the contract must never be line-ending translated.
#
# Git checks text files out as CRLF on Windows when core.autocrlf is set, which
# the GitHub Actions windows runner does by default. The report renderers emit
# LF on every platform deliberately — their output is meant to be byte-identical
# everywhere — so a translated golden file stops matching the output it pins,
# and the comparison fails on Windows and nowhere else. Checking these out as LF
# regardless of platform is what makes the goldens mean the same thing on all of
# them.
crates/report/tests/golden/** text eol=lf
